<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Clynnog Fawr</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Clynnog Fawr is a village on the north coast of the Llŷn peninsula in Gwynedd, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, associated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-beuno">Saint Beuno</a>, who founded a monastery there in the seventh century. Its clas church was one of the most important churches of medieval Gwynedd and a stopping place for pilgrims to Bardsey Island. The present large church of Saint Beuno was built in the late fifteenth and early sixteenth centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/clynnog-fawr.jpg" alt="Clynnog Fawr" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Rhion assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clynnog.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
